  <h2 id="sales">Who pays for these skills, and how they judge you</h2>

  <p>
    Employers and customers pay for skill, reliability and clear communication. Many private roles judge you by a test task and a project, not the percentage.
  </p>
  <p>
    The first basic skill is naming one skill and proving it with a small project.
  </p>

  <h2 id="ai">AI and career options after graduation with low marks: which tasks are under pressure</h2>

  <p>
    AI tools explain concepts, help practise tests and draft applications. Routine tasks shrink.
  </p>
  <p>
    Skill, honesty and proof hold value. A staged path helps: now, use AI to learn faster; later, own your results and your story.
  </p>

